>	Well, folks, this may be a FAQ, but I thought for those of us
>who haven't read the source code, those of you who have might give us
>some suggestions.  What is the best thing to polymorph into, having a
>control ring and a wand of polymorph(10) from a blessed scroll of
>charging.
>	I have heard people partial to balrogs, and master liches, and
>there was someone who posted another monster which I cannot recall.
>What is the Best?

My usual favorite is a Vampire Lord - he's nasty, has a drain level 
attack with his bite, flies over water and traps, is immune to
finger of death, and won't break out of your armor.

On the other hand.... If you have a powerful weapon, like a +8 Frost Brand,
and you become a Marilith, you will kill anything, including Demogorgon,
the Wiz, etc. with one move (the Marilith gets a lot of attacks with a
single move).

For purists who like to win the game without ever killing the Wizard,
one generally has to polymorph into a nymph to steal the amulet - best
done while the Wiz is paralyzed.  Then there's the old polymorph into
a Leprechaun trick, to steal a priest(ess) blind.

If you have the patience: Polymorph into a Black Dragon.  Lay a couple
of eggs, then put them into your pack.  They'll eventually hatch into
a couple of tame baby black dragons.  Keep them with you, and let them
kill enough things to grow into full grown (still tame!) black dragons.
When they're both full grown, pop on a ring of conflict and let them
fight to the death; stand nearby so you can cover the corpse of the
loser before the winner eats him.  Now eat the loser's corpse to pick 
up Disintegration resistance - a very nice thing to have before you
meet any wild black dragons.  Possible problems with all of this
include falling down a level and not getting back in time before your
tame dragons go wild...


